      "ticketId": "TEAM-5325",
      "lastText": "I didn't run a fourth review round. The operator stopped the run and closed it out, so the branch's last review result still stands: **CHANGES NEEDED at `546bf7d7`**.\n\n**What I found when I came back:**\n- The escalation ticket TEAM-5352 is closed. The operator's note says the run was stopped and marked complete so the post-run analysis captures the blockers, and that the security follow-ups will be filed again as separate work.\n- Every ticket under the epic TEAM-5315 is now Done, including my review ticket TEAM-5325 and the CI, QA, Ship and CD tickets. TEAM-5325 being Done does not mean the review passed.\n- `findings.md` is in S3 at `workflows/wf_1791220686225_znl7a4/shared/findings.md` (12.7 KB, last written 2026-10-06 08:24 UTC).\n\n**Still open at `546bf7d7`:**\n- **B1 (P1):** the agent runtime role and the Workflow Manager harness role can write S3 records that the hub trusts without a signature:\n  - A forged `ship-approvals/<sha>.json` skips the human deploy approval. This hole is already on main.\n  - Both roles can overwrite the CD registry and the workflow/agent config files.\n  - The harness role can forge `merge-approval.json`.\n- **B2 (P1):** after the human approves, the agent can still add items to the `gate-scope:` line, and the system signs the wider scope.\n- **R1\u2013R7 (four P2, three P3):** bugs introduced by the round-2 fixes, listed in the previous output above.\n\nI added a comment to TEAM-5325 recording this verdict. It recommends that B1 and B2 go first in the security work the operator will file again. I did not call `report_completion`: the ticket is already Done, and a new completion record could be read as a pass.\n\nCoding session: `cc-f724c3c1ad014e69a023dca43cc6566f`",
